  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This lace headband is worked flat across 18 stitches with an all-over eyelet-rib pattern, then seamed into a loop to fit adult heads of 54 to 58 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Flat construction is used because the short row count and narrow width make flat faster than in-the-round for a headband; the seam at the back is barely noticeable once blocked. Each "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "yarn-over"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "yarn over"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " pairs with a k2tog to keep the stitch count constant throughout. About 40 g (90 m) of DK yarn. Blocks to a noticeably more open, delicate fabric."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK-weight wool or wool-blend yarn",
              "qty": "40 g (approx. 90 m)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm straight or circular needle, any length (UK 8 / US 6)",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle and scissors",
              "qty": "1 each",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Measuring tape",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "22 sts x 30 rows = 10 x 10 cm in stocking stitch on 4 mm needles, blocked. At 24 sts per 10 cm the headband is 7.5 cm wide instead of 8 cm -- not critical for a headband, but check if you want a precise width. The length is governed by row count."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "k -- knit; p -- purl"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "yo -- yarn over (creates eyelet, adds 1 stitch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "k2tog -- knit 2 together (right-leaning decrease, balances yarn over)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "mattress stitch -- invisible right-side seam for finishing"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast on"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Using the long-tail cast-on, cast on 18 sts. Tail formula: tail_cm = (needle mm x stitch count) / 10 + 15. For 18 sts on a 4 mm needle: (4 x 18) / 10 + 15 = 22 cm. After cast-on, you should have 18 stitches on the needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Eyelet rib body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 1 (RS): *k2, yo, k2tog; repeat from * to last 2 sts, k2. Row 2 (WS): purl all. Repeat rows 1 and 2 until piece measures 56 cm from cast-on. After the last row, you should have 18 stitches on the needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast off"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast off all 18 sts on a WS purl row."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Common faults"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitch count growing: a yarn over was worked on a WS row by mistake, or the k2tog was missed on the RS row. Unpick to the error and re-work with the paired decrease."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Eyelets not opening after blocking: the headband was not wet-blocked. Soak in cool water for 5 minutes and lay flat to dry; the eyelets open significantly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Seam visible at back: "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mattress-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "mattress stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " worked through both layers instead of picking up the horizontal bar only. Work through the bar between edge and first stitch on each side alternately."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Wet-block the strip before seaming. Once dry, join the cast-on and cast-off edges using mattress stitch. Weave in ends."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hand wash cool, reshape and dry flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The openwork beanie uses the same eyelet repeat worked in the round for a full hat."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}